  "interpretation": {
    "positive_direction_is_text_invariant": "cos(delta measured on generic CAPTIONS, delta measured on REFUSAL text) = 0.87 at L15, 0.54-0.71 through the mid stack, falling to 0.17 at L64. Transfer confirms interchangeability: refusal-measured delta recovers 49.6/99.5/128.7% of the gap vs caption-measured 55.3/97.0/109.1%. The steering vector can be extracted from ANY text; refusal data is not required. Artifact size: ~512KB fp16 for all 50 layers, ~20KB for one layer.",
    "negative_probe_does_not_recover_it": "a difference-of-means probe (the standard steering-vector recipe) fit on base-model states correlates with the true direction at 0.23-0.48, but a LABEL-SHUFFLED probe reaches 0.14-0.33, so the margin is only 0.10-0.15. With n=26/class both are largely capturing shared assistant register. Injection: probe recovers 11.3/21.4/27.4% vs delta 55.3/97.0/109.1%, ~4x weaker.",
    "verdict": "ledger entry 4 survives in refined form: we CAN steer given a direction measured from a real edit, but our read-only instruments do not yet derive that direction themselves. Reading and steering are not the same capability here.",
    "next": "stronger probe (logistic regression, not difference of means), larger purpose-built register-matched set, and the anisotropy-corrected comparison. Also: does the direction transfer ACROSS MODEL FAMILIES, which needs a mapping since dims differ.",
    "limits": "n=26 per class; one model pair; difference-of-means is the weakest probe form."
  }
